From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:09:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] sf_smac: keep refilling the RX ring when free memory is low

Each received buffer is replaced one for one in a fixed ring of RX
buffers. The refill refused to allocate whenever free memory was under
5 MB and left the slot empty. The vendor kernel never reached that
branch, because it allocates from a private skb pool (CONFIG_SF_SKB_POOL)
that mainline does not have. On mainline the ring drains under memory
pressure until the radio stops receiving.

Drop the check and let the page allocator's watermarks decide; an
allocation failure is still counted and handled as before.

Found and measured on the Banana Pi BPI-WiFi5 by the
napoluluna/bpi-wifi5-openwrt port.

Signed-off-by: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
---
 sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/siwifi_utils.c | 6 ------
 1 file changed, 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/siwifi_utils.c b/sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/siwifi_utils.c
index 2392b8d..e7300b8 100644
--- a/sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/siwifi_utils.c
+++ b/sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/siwifi_utils.c
@@ -257,12 +257,6 @@ int siwifi_ipc_rxbuf_elem_allocs(struct siwifi_hw *siwifi_hw)
 #ifdef CONFIG_SF_SKB_POOL
     skb = __netdev_alloc_skb_from_pool(NULL, size, GFP_ATOMIC, siwifi_hw->skb_pool_dev_param);
 #else
-    unsigned long long free_mem;
-    free_mem = global_zone_page_state(NR_FREE_PAGES) << (PAGE_SHIFT -10);
-    if (free_mem < SIWIFI_RX_LOW_MEM_SIZE) {
-        siwifi_hw->rx_skb_alloc_fail_cnt++;
-        return 1;
-    }
     skb = siwifi_dev_alloc_rxskb(size);
 #endif
     if (unlikely(!skb)) {
